# elohim/elohim-agent — the agent and its gate

What belongs here: the gate crates, the agent service and its specialists, the agent SDK
sidecar, and the documents that define the gate: `spec/2026-04-18-gate-interface.md`, the
companion theory in `research/`, and the activation runbook in `gate-client/ACTIVATION.md`.

One structural fact matters when editing: `gate-client-zome` is compiled into the lamad DNA's
`content_store` coordinator zome. A change there moves no DNA hash and lands by the
coordinator hot-swap. The gate's phase is observed, never configured. A decision is stamped
`ElohimActive` only when a live model actually answered, so no flag or environment variable
should ever force it.

`covers: subtree` is a considered ownership claim with no edit-time rule.
